</ul><hr><h2>🛡️ STRIDE Analysis</h2><h3>1. <strong>S - Spoofing</strong> (Identity Theft)</h3><div class="overflow-x-auto"><table node="[object Object]" class="min-w-full"><thead><tr><th node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-2">Threat</th><th node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-2">Attack Scenario</th><th node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-2">Impact</th><th node="[object Object]" class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-2">Mitigation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2"><strong>App impersonation</strong></td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Fake app with same name on Play Store</td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Users install malicious app, data stolen</td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Use unique package name, verify developer signature</td></tr><tr><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2"><strong>User impersonation</strong></td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Employee opens owner's phone, accesses app</td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Unauthorized data access, fake entries</td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">App-level PIN/biometric lock</td></tr><tr><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2"><strong>SMS spoofing</strong></td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Attacker sends fake SMS from owner's number</td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">Customer trust lost, payment disputes</td><td node="[object Object]" class="px-3 py-2">No mitigation (SMS protocol limitation), use WhatsApp in Phase 2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Priority Mitigation:</strong></p><pre><div class="not-prose my-0 flex w-full flex-col overflow-clip border border-border text-text-primary rounded-lg not-prose relative" data-code-block="true"><div class="border-border flex items-center justify-between border-b px-4 py-2"><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg width="14" stroke-width="1.5" heigh