<li><strong>Week -2:</strong> Add feature flag in code (disabled)</li>
<li><strong>Week -1:</strong> Deploy to staging, internal testing</li>
<li><strong>Week 1:</strong> Enable for 10% users (A/B test)</li>
<li><strong>Week 2:</strong> 50% rollout if metrics good</li>
<li><strong>Week 3:</strong> 100% rollout</li>
<li><strong>Week 4:</strong> Remove feature flag code</li>
</ol><h3>Deprecated Feature Removal:</h3><ol>
<li>Mark as deprecated in code comments + logs</li>
<li>Add sunset date in API response</li>
<li>Notify users 3 months in advance</li>
<li>Remove code only after usage &lt; 1%</li>
</ol><hr><h2>Checklist Before Adding ANY New Feature</h2><ul class="contains-task-list">
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Does it break existing APIs? (If yes, version bump)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Does it need DB migration? (Plan rollback strategy)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Can it be feature-flagged? (Use flags for gradual rollout)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Is it instrumented? (Add analytics events from Day 1)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Is error handling in place? (Don't crash app if feature fails)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Is it documented? (Update ROADMAP.md + FEATURE_SPECS/)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Is it tested? (Unit + Integration tests)</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input disabled="" type="checkbox"> Is it reversible? (Can we turn it off without data loss?)</li>
</ul><hr><h2>Future Feature Preparation Checklist</h2><h3>For Phase 2 (AI Features):</h3><ul class="contains-task-list">
